{"id": "271459", "name": "שני מישורים במרחב.", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "crossprod", "params": ["x", "y"], "body": "matrix([x[2,1]*y[3,1]-x[3,1]*y[2,1]],[x[3,1]*y[1,1]-x[1,1]*y[3,1]],[x[1,1]*y[2,1]-x[2,1]*y[1,1]])"}, {"name": "norm", "params": ["x"], "body": "sqrt(x.x)"}, {"name": "proj", "params": ["x", "y"], "body": "((x.y)/(y.y))*y"}], "questiontext": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">Two planes in \\(R^3\\) assume one of three possible mutual configurations. All three are demonstrated by this little figure as follows:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"><img src=\"data/271459/files/1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"137\" height=\"174\" />    </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">(1) The planes \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) are parallel, (2) The planes \\(X\\) and \\(Z\\) intersect in a line, (3) The plane \\(X\\) coincides with itself. </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">Consider the affine plane \\(P_1\\) passing through the three points \\(u_1={{CT:0}}, u_2={{CT:1}}, u_3={{CT:2}}\\) and a second plane defined by the equation \\(P_2: \\left\\{v \\in R^3 \\ | \\ v \\cdot {{CT:3}} = {{CT:4}} \\right\\} \\). Let us investigate some geometric questions. This time we provide less information than before - leaving the tasks to you. Try to use methods similar to these that we used in the previous questions. </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">What is the cosine of the angle between the two planes (note that this is the same as the angles between the normal vectors to the two planes). </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">\\(cos(\\angle(P_1, P_2)) = \\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">What is the mutual configuration (enter a number 1=parallel, 2=intersecting, 3=coincident):</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">What is the distance between \\(P_1\\) and \\(P_2\\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]].</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>", "generalfeedback": "", "specificfeedback": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">[[feedback:prt2]]</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">[[feedback:prt3]] </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">[[feedback:prt4]]</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans4", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "sang:sqrt(1-chang^2);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "cang", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">You found the correct cosine of the angle between the line and the normal vector. </p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "-cang", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-2-T", "feedback": "<p dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">You found the correct cosine of the angle between the line and the normal vector. </p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "-", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-2-F", "feedback": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">No this is not the correct cosine of the angle between the two planes. </p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "choice", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">Yes, you found the correct mutual configuration of \\(P\\) and \\(\\ell\\). </p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\">No, you did not find the correct mutual configuration of \\(P\\) and \\(\\ell\\). Please try again.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt4", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "vec:matrix([x],[y],[z]);", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans4", "tans": "d", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt4-1-T", "feedback": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"ltr\"> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\" dir=\"l